From 07404fad4b4912cdf26a2e3abbcb14030942bb88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wang Emma <wangzhn>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:39:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] feat(swarm): subagents inherit the parent's permission
 overlay and definition limits

A subagent started by the agent tool runs as a --task-worker process that
only read the global settings.json. A worker restricted through --settings
could therefore escape its rules by spawning a subagent. The child now
gets:

- the parent's SettingsOverlay (rebuilt with SettingsOverlay.to_cli_args):
  path rules, denied commands, writable paths, tool lists and MCP servers;
- the parent's permission mode, unless the definition sets one;
- the definition's own limits. disallowed_tools, plus every available tool
  missing from a tools allowlist, are denied. permissions are granted as
  allowed tools.

Built-in definitions use Claude Code tool names (Read, file_edit, ...),
which never matched the registry, so normalize_tool_name maps them to
read_file, edit_file, ... first. Definition permission modes map to
OpenHarness modes: bypassPermissions/dontAsk -> full_auto,
acceptEdits -> default. Previously acceptEdits would have crashed the
child.

build_inherited_cli_flags no longer shlex-quotes values. The flags are an
argv for direct exec, and the quotes ended up inside the values (e.g. the
subagent system prompt).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
